nt === 3 && !liveSet.has(key)) {\n      const [nx, ny] = key.split(\",\").map(Number) as [number, number];\n      result.push([nx, ny]);\n    }\n  }\n\n  return result;\n}\n```\n\n**Component Count**:\n\n| Component | Occurrences | Mass |\n|-----------|-------------|------|\n| **Constants (×1)** | `\",\"` × 3, `-1` × 2, `1` × 2, `0` × 3, `2`, `3` = 13 | 13 |\n| **Bindings (×1)** | `cells`, `liveSet`, `neighborCounts`, `x`, `y`, `dx`, `dy`, `key`, `result`, `count`, `nx`, `ny` = 12 | 12 |\n| **Invocations (×2)** | `Set()`, `cells.map()`, `Map()`, `neighborCounts.set()`, `neighborCounts.get()` ×2, `+` ×4 (x+dx, y+dy, +1, map split coords), `result.push()` ×2, `liveSet.has()`, `key.split()`, `.map(Number)` = 16 | 32 |\n| **Conditionals (×4)** | `dx===0 && dy===0`, `count===2 || count===3`, `count===3 && !liveSet.has()` = 3 | 12 |\n| **Loops (×5)** | Outer `for of cells`, nested `for dx`, nested `for dy`, survival `for of cells`, reproduction `for of neighborCounts` = 5 | 25 |\n| **Assignments (×6)** | `dx++`, `dy++` = 2 | 12 |\n\n**Total Mass: 13 + 12 + 32 + 12 + 25 + 12 = 106**\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: Before/After Comparison\n\n| Component | Before | After | Delta |\n|-----------|--------|-------|-------|\n| Constants | ~25 | 13 | -12 |\n| Bindings | ~14 | 12 | -2 |\n| Invocations | ~18 (×2=36) | 16 (×2=32) | -4 |\n| Conditionals | 5 (×4=20) | 3 (×4=12) | -8 |\n| Loops | 7 (×5=35) | 5 (×5=25) | -10 |\n| Assignments | 6 (×6=36) | 2 (×6=12) | -24 |\n| **Total** | **~166** | **106** | **-60** |\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: Document Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n\n1. **Eliminated the duplicated neighbor-offset loop**: The old code had the same nested `dx/dy` loop in two places (`countNeighbors` function and dead-candidate collection). Now there's just one.\n\n2. **Merged counting into a single pre-computation pass**: Instead of computing neighbors on-demand for each dead candidate (which meant re-scanning from scratch), all neighbor counts are computed in one pass into a `Ma