(which meant re-scanning from scratch), all neighbor counts are computed in one pass into a `Map<string, number>`. The survival and reproduction phases then simply read from this map.\n\n3. **Removed the `countNeighbors` inner function**: No longer needed since the count is pre-computed.\n\n4. **Reduced from 7 loops to 5 loops**: Before: outer `for of cells`, `countNeighbors` nested dx/dy (3 more), dead-candidate nested dx/dy (2 more), reproduction `for of deadCandidates`. After: outer `for of cells` with nested dx/dy (3), survival `for of cells`, reproduction `for of neighborCounts`.\n\n5. **Reduced assignments from ~6 to 2**: The `count++` and the dead-candidate collection are replaced by the map lookup + set pattern.\n\n**Benefits**:\n- **Single knowledge source**: The 8-neighbor iteration only appears once\n- **Cleaner separation**: Survival and reproduction logic are clearly separated into distinct phases\n- **Lower mass**: Reduced from ~166 to 106 (mass reduction of ~60, approximately 36%)\n- **All tests pass**: No regression\n- **Name `nextGeneration` maintained**: Still clear and appropriate\n\n**Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: Maintained — the three distinct phases (count neighbors, apply survival, apply reproduction) are now clearly separated with explicit comments.\n\n**Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: ✓ Improved — the duplicated neighbor-offset loop is now a single occurrence.\n\n---\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring**: Eliminated duplicated neighbor-offset loop and removed dynamic `countNeighbors` function; replaced with single-pass neighbor-counting via `Map`, and separated survival/reproduction phases.  \n**Mass Change**: ~166 → 106 (delta -60, ~36% reduction)  \n**Tests**: All 5 passing, 2 todo remain."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_12-14-27_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/game-of-life.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/game-of-life.ts\nPassing tests: 5\nRecent Green phase: Added reproduction logic — dead cells adjacent to live cells with exactly 3 neighbors are born.\n\nRun autonomously, return after completion.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/game-of-life.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/game-of-life.ts\nPassing tests: 5\nRecent Green phase: Added reproduction logic — dead cells adjacent to live cells with exactly 3 neighbors are born.\n\nRun autonomously, return after completion."}],"timestamp":1784981766640},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'll start by reading the current implementation and test files to understand the"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_59829be44bb149719582062a","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/game-of-life.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_467d9fd7ae4d40c684ea1405","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/game-of-life.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":139,"output":101,"cacheRead":6656,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":6896,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784981766665,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-89f15797-3b86-4b0e-a8f4-a0db389ca3d7","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_59829be44bb149719582062a","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export function nextGeneration(cells: [number, number][]): [number, number][] {\n  // Build a set of live cells for O(1) lookup\n  const liveSet = new Set(cells.map(([x, y]) => `${x},${y}`));\n\n  // Count neighbors for a given cell\n  const countNeighbors = (x: number, y: number): number => {\n    let count = 0;\n    for (let dx = -1; dx <= 1; dx++) {\n      for (let dy = -1; dy <= 1; dy++) {\n        if (dx === 0 && dy === 0) continue;\n        if (liveSet.has(`${x + dx},${y + dy}`)) {\n          count++;\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    return count;\n  };\n\n  const result: [number, number][] = [];\n  const deadCandidates = new Set<string>();\n\n  for (const [x, y] of cells) {\n    const neighbors = countNeighbors(x, y);\n    // Survival: live cell with 2 or 3 neighbors lives on\n    if (neighbors === 2 || neighbors === 3) {\n      result.push([x, y]);\n    }\n\n    // Collect dead neighbor positions as reproduction candidates\n    for (let dx = -1; dx <= 1; dx++) {\n      for (let dy = -1; dy <= 1; dy++) {\n        if (dx === 0 && dy === 0) continue;\n        const nx = x + dx;\n        const ny = y + dy;\n        if (!liveSet.has(`${nx},${ny}`)) {\n          deadCandidates.add(`${nx},${ny}`);\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Check dead candidates for reproduction\n  for (const key of deadCandidates) {\n    const [nx, ny] = key.split(\",\").map(Number) as [number, number];\n    if (countNeighbors(nx, ny) === 3) {\n      result.push([nx, ny]);\n    }\n  }\n\n  return result;\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784981767460},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_467d9fd7ae4d40c684ea1405","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { nextGeneration } from \"./game-of-life.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Game of Life - Next Generation\", () => {\n  // Simplest case: single cell dies (no neighbors)\n  it(\"should kill a single live cell with no neighbors -- Gen 0: [(0,0)] -> Gen 1: []\", () => {\n    expect(nextGeneration([[0, 0]])).toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  // Rule 1 – Underpopulation: live cell with < 2 neighbors dies\n  it(\"should kill two live cells each with only 1 neighbor (underpopulation) -- Gen 0: [(0,1), (1,1)] -> Gen 1: []\", () => {\n    expect(nextGeneration([[0, 1], [1, 1]])).toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  // Rule 2 – Survival: live cell with 2 or 3 neighbors lives on\n  it(\"should keep a live cell alive with 2 neighbors (survival) -- horizontal line of 3 with births above and below\", () => {\n    // Three in a horizontal line: (0,0),(1,0),(2,0)\n    // (1,0) has 2 neighbors: (0,0) and (2,0) -> survives\n    // (0,0) has 1 neighbor: (1,0) -> dies\n    // (2,0) has 1 neighbor: (1,0) -> dies\n    // (1,-1) dead with neighbors (0,0),(1,0),(2,0)=3 -> born\n    // (1,1) dead with neighbors (0,0),(1,0),(2,0)=3 -> born\n    const result = nextGeneration([[0, 0], [1, 0], [2, 0]]);\n    expect(result).toEqual([[1, 0], [1, -1], [1, 1]]);\n  });\n\n  // Rule 3 – Overpopulation: live cell with > 3 neighbors dies\n  it(\"should kill a cell with 4 neighbors (overpopulation) -- center cell with 4 neighbors dies\", () => {\n    // Center (0,0) with 4 neighbors: (1,0), (-1,0), (0,1), (0,-1)\n    // (0,0) has 4 neighbors -> dies (overpopulation)\n    const result = nextGeneration([[-1, 0], [1, 0], [0, -1], [0, 1], [0, 0]]);\n    // Verify center (0,0) is NOT in result\n    const hasCenter = result.some(([x, y]) => x === 0 && y === 0);\n    expect(hasCenter).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  // Rule 4 – Reproduction: dead cell with exactly 3 neighbors becomes alive\n  it(\"should reproduce a dead cell with exactly 3 live neighbors -- Gen 0: [(0,0), (1,0), (0,1)] -> Gen 1 includes (1,1)\", () => {\n    // Three cells forming an L-shape: (0,0), (1,0), (0,1)\n    // Dead cell (1,1) has 3 live neighbors -> becomes alive\n    // Live cells: (0,0) - 1 neighbor (1,0) or check...\n    // (0,0) neighbors: (1,0), (0,1) = 2 -> survives\n    // (1,0) neighbors: (0,0), (0,1) = 2 -> survives\n    // (0,1) neighbors: (0,0), (1,0) = 2 -> survives\n    // (1,1) dead, neighbors: (0,0), (1,0), (0,1) = 3 -> born\n    const result = nextGeneration([[0, 0], [1, 0], [0, 1]]);\n    expect(result).toEqual(expect.arrayContaining([[1, 1]]));\n    expect(result).toHaveLength(4);\n  });\n\n  // Pattern example: Block (still life)\n  it.todo(\"should keep a 2x2 block unchanged (still life) -- Gen 0: [(0,0), (1,0), (0,1), (1,1)] -> Gen 1: same\");\n\n  /